<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xiongnu civil war</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">57 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a> civil war was a succession conflict among rival claimants to the position of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chanyu">chanyu</a> that split the Xiongnu Empire around 57 BCE. The confederation divided between factions led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huhanye">Huhanye</a>, who submitted to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a>, and his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhizhi">Zhizhi</a>, who moved westward. Accounts of the Xiongnu Empire treat this split as a major stage in the empire's decline.</p></div>
